\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Three-layer block diagram of Project Garuda. Top: inference pipeline (camera $\to $ GStreamer $\to $ Hailo-8L $\to $ detection classes). Middle: response and control (alert engine, Narada voice assistant, mode controller, presence monitor). Bottom: persistence and external communication (FastAPI + Cloudflare tunnel, authentication, deadman watchdog, multi-tier logging).}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:block_diagram}{{1}{3}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Project Garuda end-to-end flowchart. Video enters the GStreamer TAPPAS pipeline; YOLOv8s runs on the Hailo-8L NPU; post-inference detections are routed through watch/danger classification and a mode gate that fans out into email, WebSocket, and encrypted clip upload. Parallel subsystems (voice assistant, presence monitor, deadman watchdog, mode scheduler, authentication, and the Cloudflare-tunnelled web server) execute concurrently and feed the multi-tier logging engine.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:system_flowchart}{{2}{4}}
